hazard zone is battlefield 2042's new  squad based competitive mode and it  honestly sounded pretty complicated on  the dice blog but it's really not at the  most basic level it's about finding hard  drives and getting out on an aircraft  alive but there's also a ton of ways to  do that and we're here to help you out  with what we learned so far hit that  subscribe button bang on the old thumbs  up and let's dive into hazard zone  number one start early seriously if you  think this is your jam don't wait to  play hazard zone that's because you  currently start with zero dark market  credits that's the currency used to buy  weapons and powerful upgrades before  each round earned from the previous  round that means if you start late you  risk getting rolled by fully kitted  teams who've been playing for a while  that's one of the things that makes this  not like battle royale you do start each  round with stuff number two grunt  farming is a viable strategy if you just  ignored that first tip there's more than  one way to earn dark market credits and  data drives aren't worth as much as you  might think if you die before extracting  with hard drives you lose those points  but you still keep what you earn from  killing opposing forces the enemy bots  and also other enemy teams for free you  can even equip the negotiated bounty one  perk that gives you fifty percent more  returns for grunt farming as a matter of  fact if you're just going to extract  with a few hard drives you can probably  make as much by just fighting since  there's only eight other teams it could  be a viable strategy to just go hunt  them down and take the drives that they  drop  number three when you come across  satellites or an opposing force you  might want to hang back and see what  happens like in any battle royale ish  mode you can and will get third partied  at the worst possible time number four  bring ammo ammo management is  challenging across most of the major  modes in 2042 and if you start fights  you will run out either buy ammo crates  at the start of rounds bring angel or  just be very mindful of when to break  off and save your ammo for an extraction  i did run out several times another tip  is to buy weapons at the start of each  round that come with different ammo  types because each magazine has its own  ammo count so if you run out of one type  you have backups another great way to  save ammo is to let boris's turret and  ranger do some of the work for you when  it comes to killing opposing forces  number five some specialists can work a  little different in hazard zone like  angel who can't seem to do his one thing  dropping a crate that lets you swap  loadouts because you don't have multiple  loadouts in these matches that being  said specialists do have some major  advantages boris's sentry turret is not  great at killing but it's fantastic at  alerting you to enemies around you and  could keep you from getting third  partied all about that situational  awareness  number six on the topic of loadouts make  sure you get your guns out in the plus  system because you're really buying your  own weapons at the start of each round  that means the more unlocked your guns  are from all out warfare the better they  are in hazard zone number seven pack a  dmr or get yourself with a gun that's  good at range a lot of these maps are  huge with long sight lines so good  snipers are probably going to grow  dominant in hazard zone be one of them  number eight buy insurance at the start  of every round you can buy more than  just guns you can actually buy insurance  which gives you back some of your dark  market credits at the end of a round  although i have to say in our experience  one big win will carry you several  rounds afterwards number nine be on mic  although update you'll have to be on  discord or other services until voice  chat is actually added into the game  later on i seriously can't imagine this  mode without a coordinated squad the  ping system is pretty good at calling  out specific info like what you spotted  the direction and the range but it just  can't make up for the kind of  communication you need in an actual  fight like when to hold back or when to  push a team that's weak it also just  can't do things like conversations you  need to have like should you go to the  first condor or wait for the second  games like warzone have made huge  strides for solo players in recent years  and hazard zone just doesn't have a solo  rando friendly environment at least at  launch another thing to keep in mind  though if you're communicating is  there's a pretty good compass now which  you can use for good call outs number 10  vehicles are both power and risk this  will be a few points on vehicles but  vehicles in 2042 are very strong in  multiple modes and that's no different  for hazard zone calling in some kind of  fast transport vehicle that has a gun on  top can make or break around you can  literally just roll up on squads that  are unprepared and demolish them number  11 make sure someone on your team is an  anti-vehicle specialist like sundance or  bring a rocket it will save you number  12 which is why no squad should all pile  into one vehicle seriously just don't do  it your game might end real fast if you  get hit but in a pinch if you all have  to pile into one truck you can get  creative but dozer in the flatbed with  his shield out to protect your team's  back also riding in the flap out of the  truck is the only way to shoot enemy  teams chasing you you can't turn around  in the front seats number 13 calling the  dogs and more the call and tablet is  just as powerful here as it is in all  out warfare as you roam the map you'll  find things like ranger call-ins team  respawn uplinks and vehicle drops your  team can call in multiple rangers at  once and they'll follow you for the rest  of the match they're fantastic at  alerting you of enemy teams and opposing  forces nearby but on the other side of  that rangers are really bad at stealth  and they'll alert everyone to your  presence by shooting at anything that  moves even at pretty far distances we  haven't found a way to tell them to just  not  found danger 260 degrees  14 let's talk about extractions for  starters you can't blow up the condor we  did ask you should though always assume  there's an enemy team already inside we  won a couple of matches when other teams  strolled up to the condor unaware we  were in there so if you're approaching  one always throw a grenade or fire a  rocket into it first that or use one of  the wall hack characters like pake to  scan the condor before entering number  15 you can't plug the doorway with dozer  shield or irish's barricade we tried it  and it seemed kind of buggy it didn't  work for some reason but it's a great  idea to leave boris's turret or irish's  barricade outside for some added cover  number 16 don't forget to have someone  hang back if you have a lot to lose  while you're playing keep looking for  squad redeploy uplinks around the map  they can be used to bring your squad  back to life through the calling tablet  if you're on a streak and have a lot of  hard drives and are looking to get more  someone should stay behind with a squad  redeploy on blake just in case it goes  bad keep in mind though there's a pretty  long squad redeploy timer and everyone  will definitely see you parachute back  in number 17 don't forget if you go down  but not out you drop hard drives you're  carrying if your squad comes out on top  remember to pick them back up likewise  scavenge enemy teams for their drives  number 18. remember how the blog said  only two teams can extract that's not  exactly true you can still get on the  condor in the down but not out state and  extract although you won't get credit  for the drives you dropped i imagine  also two squads can just not shoot each  other and both extract if they want and  if you do make it the game has  extraction streaks the impact of that is  that at the start of every round you  only get one tactical slot but the more  you extract the more tactical slots open  up each subsequent round and that lets  you buy more tools for each following  round that kind of incentivizes people  to take the first condor out if you're  playing battlefield 2042 we can't wait  to see what you find in hazard zone  seriously we got a lot of testing to do  so give us your best tips in the  comments below while you're at it don't  forget to head on over to gamespot's  youtube page to check out our review in  progress and with that let's leave you  with some gameplay of one intense  extraction we came across in our review  event thanks for watching  oh  [Music]  [ __ ]  we'll do better next time  ah this is what i expected
 

